note The step entry point. Sets the path and step (and the step as the target), expands every collapsed ancestor of the step so the document shows it, focuses the step's symbol and selects its lines, asks the document to scroll the header to the top unless the click was inside the document, and turns a Source, Search or Diff tab into the Path tab. A step over lines with no symbol of their own focuses the symbol around those lines, so the References panel still has something to show.

